# Git: push to `main` by default

For this repository, when the user asks to save work, push changes, ship, or complete a task that includes git:

1. Commit any pending changes on the current branch with a clear message.
2. Ensure **`main`** includes the work (merge or commit directly on `main` as appropriate).
3. Run **`git push origin main`** without asking for separate confirmation, unless the user explicitly wants a feature branch, draft PR only, or no push.

If the user says they do not want to be asked about pushing next time, treat that as this policy until they say otherwise.
